{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/init()"],"title":"Creating a Command Buffer","anchor":"Creating-a-Command-Buffer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/count","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/isEmpty"],"title":"Inspecting a Command Buffer","anchor":"Inspecting-a-Command-Buffer"},{"anchor":"Spawning-and-Despawning-Entities","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/clone(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/despawn(_:)"],"title":"Spawning and Despawning Entities"},{"anchor":"Adding-and-Removing-Components","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(_:into:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/remove(_:from:)"],"title":"Adding and Removing Components"},{"anchor":"Changing-the-Hierarchy-and-Relations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/addChild(_:to:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/removeParent(of:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/relate(_:_:to:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/unrelate(_:_:from:)"],"title":"Changing the Hierarchy and Relations"},{"anchor":"Sending-Events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/send(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/trigger(_:on:)"],"title":"Sending Events"},{"anchor":"Changing-Resources","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(resource:)"],"title":"Changing Resources"},{"anchor":"Recording-Any-Change","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/record(_:)"],"title":"Recording Any Change"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a query or an update visits a world’s entities, the world can’t be changed in other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ways: spawning or despawning an entity, or adding or removing a component, would disturb the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage being visited. Record such changes in a command buffer instead, and apply them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" once the visit is over. The following example despawns every entity whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"health has run out:"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","for (entity, health) in world.query(Health.self) where health.current <= 0 {","    commands.despawn(entity)","}","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A command on an entity that is no longer live when it applies does nothing, so two commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that despawn the same entity are safe.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Naming Entities That Commands Will Spawn","level":3,"anchor":"Naming-Entities-That-Commands-Will-Spawn","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns a placeholder handle for the entity it will create. Later commands in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same buffer can name that placeholder, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the real handles of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entities it spawned, in the order their commands were recorded:"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","var commands = Commands()","let ship = commands.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let turret = commands.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 0))","commands.addChild(turret, to: ship)","","let spawned = world.apply(commands)","print(world.parent(of: spawned[1]) == spawned[0])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A placeholder stands for its entity only inside the buffer that returned it; the world holds no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity with that handle."}]},{"text":"Commands from Systems","level":3,"anchor":"Commands-from-Systems","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A system running alongside others can’t apply commands itself, because applying them would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change entities the other systems are reading. It queues them with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead, and the schedule applies every queued buffer at the end of each wave of systems.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recorded.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Commands.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Commands.swift#L55"},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","title":"Commands","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Commands/remove(_:from:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/remove(_:from:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"remove(_:from:)","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands\/remove(_:from:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remove","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"B","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"B","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV","text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records removing from an entity every component type a bundle can hold."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://